; psk31_tx.loom
; A PSK31 transmitter (amateur-radio keyboard mode, G3PLX): text from the
; host, varicode coded, sent as binary phase-shift keying of an audio
; carrier at 31.25 baud on one pin, with a preamble of reversals before the
; text and a postamble of steady carrier after it. Two modes: a square-wave
; carrier with abrupt reversals, or a sine carrier whose reversals are
; cosine-shaped, as a one-bit sigma-delta stream for an RC low-pass.
;
; Written on 2026-11-07, after the hardware was complete (D-032), as a
; protocol Loom was not designed for (D-035). PSK31 is not a line code but
; a narrow-band phase modulation of an audio tone, and nothing in Loom was
; built for it: no oscillator, no DAC, no modulator, no multiplier. The
; program uses:
;   - the per-thread fractional tick (TICK_INT/TICK_FRAC, built for UART
;     baud rates) as the sample clock: one output bit per tick;
;   - the deadline schedule (WAITD 1 every sample, proved by the checker);
;   - the data memory (LD/ST, built for device-emulation tables) for the
;     varicode table, a 64-entry sine table and the transmitter's state;
;   - OUT through a one-pin OUTGRP group (as dtmf_gen.loom), so every
;     sample's bit lands the same number of clocks after its tick.
; What the firmware does that no hardware does: the varicode, the carrier
; NCO, the BPSK, the cosine shaping of each reversal, the sigma-delta
; modulation, the preamble, the idle between characters, the postamble and
; the key-up and key-down ramps.
;
; Sources (tools/protomodels/psk31.py gives them in full): the ARRL "PSK31
; Spec" page (N5SK after G3PLX): 31.25 baud; 0 = phase reversal, 1 = steady
; carrier; the output cosine-filtered; preamble = continuous zeros (idle),
; postamble = unmodulated carrier (ones); at least two zeros between
; characters. The varicode table is fldigi's (pskvaricode.cxx), checked row
; by row against the ARRL table (which has rows 90..96 shifted by one). G3PLX's
; own RadCom article (1998/99) could not be read: unchecked.
;
; The shaping, and why no multiplier is needed. A reversal shaped by a
; cosine is cos(pi t / T) sin(wc t) over one symbol T, centred on the
; boundary; by the product formula that is half the sum of two tones,
; sin(wc t + pi t / T) + sin(wc t - pi t / T) (G3PLX's two-tone picture).
; So the program keeps a carrier phase th_c and a modulation phase th_m and
; outputs  sin(th_c + th_m) + sin(th_c - th_m) = 2 sin(th_c) cos(th_m):
; th_m resting at 0 or 1/2 cycle is the carrier with sign + or -, th_m
; moving by 1/2 cycle over one symbol is a cosine-shaped reversal, and th_m
; at 1/4 cycle is no carrier at all. Two table look-ups and an add.
;
; Square mode: the pin is the sign of sin(th_c + th_m), and th_m jumps by
; 1/2 cycle exactly at a symbol boundary. This is plain square-wave BPSK:
; its spectrum is a sinc around the carrier (sidebands at fc +- 1.5, 2.5 ..
; times the baud rate only about 10, 14 .. dB down) plus the square wave's
; odd harmonics: much wider than PSK31's two tones, as test_fw_psk31.py
; measures. Use it only into a narrow filter, or where width does not
; matter.
;
; Shaped mode: x = 32768 + 32000 sin(th_c) cos(th_m) (two words of
; dtmf_gen.loom's table, 16384 + round(16000 sin)), first-order
; sigma-delta: the carry of a 16-bit accumulator is the pin. An RC low-pass
; (for example 1 kohm, 47 nF) gives the audio for a transceiver's input.
; The reversal's envelope is exactly a cosine sampled N times; its zero
; is the symbol boundary, N/2 samples after the program's decision instant
; (the symbol centre). Phase truncation to 6 bits and the modulator's
; noise are the only impurities; test_fw_psk31.py measures the result.
;
; Sample grid. fs = clock / tick. A symbol is N samples, N a power of two
; (the host gives it), so the ramp step 32768 / N is exact and th_m lands
; on its rest values exactly. The carrier is STEP / 65536 cycles a sample.
; At 50 MHz, for 1000 Hz and 31.25 baud exactly:
;     fs 32 000 Hz: TICK_INT 1562, TICK_FRAC 128, N 1024, STEP 2048
;     fs 128 000 Hz: TICK_INT 390, TICK_FRAC 160, N 4096, STEP 512
; Shaped mode wants the second: a first-order sigma-delta driven by a
; signal that repeats every two symbols (idle) has idle tones on the very
; lines that measure PSK31's purity (fc +- 3/2 baud, "IMD"): measured about
; -23 to -30 dB at 32 samples a carrier cycle, -50 dB or lower at 128
; (test_fw_psk31.py). Square mode does not care. The rate and
; the carrier are both exact to the board clock. The schedule is proved
; for any tick of at least the .tick below.
;
; Host interface (FIFO space, thread 0):
;   INQ, first five words (configuration): STEP; N (a power of two, 4 or
;     more); MODE (bit 0: 1 shaped, 0 square); PRE, the preamble in symbols
;     (zeros); POST, the postamble in symbols (ones).
;   INQ, then: one word a character: bits 6:0 the character (bit 7 and
;     bits 15:9 ignored); bit 8 set: end of message (postamble, key down).
;   A word queued while the carrier is off keys up: a reference symbol
;   (square) or a half-symbol cosine ramp-up (shaped), then the preamble,
;   then the text. While the queue is empty the transmitter sends idle
;   (zeros, which is also how PSK31 idles between characters). An end word
;   queued while off sends a preamble and a postamble and nothing between.
;   After the postamble: square mode stops at once (pin low); shaped mode
;   ramps the carrier down over half a symbol (cosine), then silence (the
;   pin alternates 1, 0: the filter's mid level). Nothing goes to OUTQ.
;
; Pins: TX = OUT0 (any output with --pin TX=<pin>).
;
; Memory: 354 words in 0x000 .. 0x16F (.imem 512): variables 0x001 ..
; 0x00B, configuration code to 0x030, the sine table 0x040 .. 0x07F (an
; absolute address, as dtmf_gen.loom: ADDI 63 then LD +1), the rest of the
; code 0x080 .. 0x0EF, the varicode table 0x0F0 .. 0x16F. That is threads 0
; to 2's quarters: threads 1 and 2 cannot run beside it, thread 3 (0x180)
; can, with up to 128 words of its own. The varicode table is most of it;
; a printable-only table (32 .. 127 and CR, LF) would bring the program
; inside two quarters (QUESTIONS).
;
; Deadlines: ten pairs, all proved, one POP bounded by declaration (it
; follows a WAITB INQ_NE, T that completed by its condition). The worst is
; a shaped sample whose decision ends the preamble and pops and looks up
; the first character: 75 slots = 300 clocks, the .tick below; at 50 MHz
; fs 32 kHz gives a tick of 1562.5 clocks and fs 128 kHz 390.6.
;
; Readings taken on the open spec questions (2026-11-07): varicode from the
; ARRL "PSK31 Spec" table checked row by row against fldigi's table (the
; ARRL table shifts rows 90 to 96 by one); G3PLX's RadCom article was not
; read. Secondary.
;   Use shaped mode at 128 k samples a second (TICK_INT 390, TICK_FRAC
;   160 at 50 MHz) on the air: square mode is as wide as textbook square
;   BPSK (first sidebands -8.8 dB). Shaped mode's limit is the
;   first-order sigma-delta's idle tones (-50 dB and below at that rate).
;   Preamble and postamble lengths are host words (the source gives
;   none). Only codes 0 to 127 are sent.

        .imem   512
        .thread 0
        .pins   TX = OUT0
        .tick   300
        .equ    SINE  = 0x40                    ; 64 words, 16384 + round(16000 sin(2 pi i / 64))
        .equ    EMPTY = 0x8000                  ; SR holding only its stop marker
        .equ    ZERO1 = 0x4000                  ; SR for one 0 (idle, preamble)
        .equ    ONE1  = 0xC000                  ; SR for one 1 (postamble)
        .equ    QUART = 16384                   ; th_m of the envelope zero

; r0 th_c, the carrier phase (2^16 = one cycle)   r1 th_m, the modulation phase
; r2 STEP   r3 th_m's step this symbol (0, or 32768 / N while a shaped
; reversal runs)   r4 the sigma-delta accumulator   r5 the next sample's bit
; r6 r7 scratch; r7 the samples left in the symbol inside the loops.
        JMP     start
NWORD:  .word   0                               ; N, samples a symbol
KEYLEN: .word   0                               ; key-up and key-down segment: N/2 shaped, N square
MODE:   .word   0                               ; 1 shaped, 0 square
THETA0: .word   0                               ; th_m at key-up: QUART shaped, 0 square
IMM0:   .word   0                               ; th_m's jump on a 0: 32768 square, 0 shaped
RAMP0:  .word   0                               ; th_m's step on a 0: 32768 / N shaped, 0 square
PRE:    .word   0                               ; preamble symbols
POST:   .word   0                               ; postamble symbols
CNT:    .word   0                               ; preamble or postamble symbols left
STATE:  .word   0                               ; 1 preamble, 2 text, 3 postamble, 4 ramp-down
SR:     .word   EMPTY                           ; bits still to send, MSB next, then a stop 1

start:  .csr    OUTGRP, (1 << 5) | pin(TX)      ; OUT r writes r[0] to TX
        LDI     r6, 0                           ; the base of every variable
        POP     r2                              ; STEP (blocks)
        POP     r7                              ; N (blocks)
        ST      r7, r6, NWORD
        MOV16   r3, 0x8000                      ; 32768 / N, N a power of two
        MOV     r5, r7
rdiv:   SHRI    r5, 1
        BZ      rdone
        SHRI    r3, 1
        JMP     rdiv
rdone:  POP     r5                              ; MODE (blocks)
        ANDI    r5, 1
        ST      r5, r6, MODE
        BZ      sqcfg
        ST      r3, r6, RAMP0                   ; shaped: a 0 ramps th_m by 32768 over N
        ST      r6, r6, IMM0
        MOV16   r3, QUART
        ST      r3, r6, THETA0                  ; key up from the envelope zero
        SHRI    r7, 1                           ; and ramp up over N/2 samples
        JMP     cfg2
sqcfg:  ST      r6, r6, RAMP0                   ; square: a 0 jumps th_m by 32768
        ST      r6, r6, THETA0
        MOV16   r3, 0x8000
        ST      r3, r6, IMM0
cfg2:   ST      r7, r6, KEYLEN
        POP     r7                              ; PRE (blocks)
        ST      r7, r6, PRE
        POP     r7                              ; POST (blocks)
        ST      r7, r6, POST
        LDI     r5, 0
        SETD    1
        JMP     off

        .org    SINE                            ; 16384 + round(16000 sin(2 pi i / 64))
        .word   16384, 17952, 19505, 21029, 22507, 23926, 25273, 26534
        .word   27698, 28752, 29688, 30495, 31166, 31695, 32077, 32307
        .word   32384, 32307, 32077, 31695, 31166, 30495, 29688, 28752
        .word   27698, 26534, 25273, 23926, 22507, 21029, 19505, 17952
        .word   16384, 14816, 13263, 11739, 10261,  8842,  7495,  6234
        .word    5070,  4016,  3080,  2273,  1602,  1073,   691,   461
        .word     384,   461,   691,  1073,  1602,  2273,  3080,  4016
        .word    5070,  6234,  7495,  8842, 10261, 11739, 13263, 14816


; Carrier off. Square: the pin low. Shaped: 1, 0, 1, 0 (x = 32768, the
; filter's mid level). The pending bit goes out first. Any queued word
; keys up; it is popped later, in the text state.
off:    LDI     r6, 0
        LD      r6, r6, MODE
offl:   WAITD   1
        OUT     r5
        XOR     r5, r5, r6
        AND     r5, r5, r6
        WAITB   INQ_NE, T                       ; TD has passed: a test, not a wait
        BT      offl
        LDI     r6, 0                           ; key up
        LD      r7, r6, PRE
        ST      r7, r6, CNT
        LDI     r7, 1
        ST      r7, r6, STATE
        LDI     r0, 0                           ; th_c from 0: boundaries at th_c = 0
        LD      r1, r6, THETA0
        LD      r3, r6, RAMP0
        LD      r7, r6, KEYLEN
        JMP     loop

; Pick the sample loop of the mode; r6 must be 0 here.
loop:   LD      r6, r6, MODE
        TEST    r6, r6
        BZ      sqloop
        JMP     shloop

; One square-mode sample: the bit for this sample (computed last tick) goes
; out right after the tick; then the sign of sin(th_c + th_m) for the next.
sqloop: WAITD   1
        OUT     r5
        MOV     r5, r0
        ADD     r5, r5, r1
        SHRI    r5, 15                          ; 1 in the negative half-cycle
        ADD     r0, r0, r2
        DJNZ    r7, sqloop
        JMP     sym

; One shaped sample: out with the bit computed last tick, then
; x = t[th_c + th_m] + t[th_c - th_m] = 32768 + 32000 sin(th_c) cos(th_m)
; into the modulator; its carry is the next bit. 21 slots and the WAITD.
shloop: WAITD   1
        OUT     r5
        MOV     r5, r0
        ADD     r5, r5, r1
        SHRI    r5, 10                          ; the top 6 bits
        ADDI    r5, 63
        LD      r5, r5, SINE - 63
        MOV     r6, r0
        SUB     r6, r6, r1
        SHRI    r6, 10
        ADDI    r6, 63
        LD      r6, r6, SINE - 63
        ADD     r5, r5, r6                      ; x, 768 .. 64768
        ADD     r4, r4, r5                      ; C = the bit
        CSRR    r5, FLAGS                       ; {T, C, Z}
        SHRI    r5, 1                           ; r5[0] = C
        ADD     r0, r0, r2
        ADD     r1, r1, r3
        DJNZ    r7, shloop

; A decision instant (square: a symbol boundary; shaped: a symbol centre,
; N/2 samples before the boundary its reversal straddles). The last sample
; is computed and in r5; everything below fits in the same tick.
sym:    LDI     r6, 0
        LD      r7, r6, SR
        SHLI    r7, 1                           ; C = the next bit
        BZ      refill                          ; only the stop 1 was left
have:   ST      r7, r6, SR
        LDI     r3, 0                           ; a 1: no reversal (LDI keeps C)
        BC      next
        LD      r3, r6, IMM0                    ; a 0: square, the reversal now;
        ADD     r1, r1, r3
        LD      r3, r6, RAMP0                   ; shaped, over the next N samples
next:   LD      r7, r6, NWORD
        JMP     loop

refill: LD      r7, r6, STATE
        CMPI    r7, 2
        BZ      text
        BC      late                            ; 3 postamble or 4 ramp-down
        LD      r7, r6, CNT                     ; 1: preamble
        SUBI    r7, 1                           ; C = a symbol left
        BNC     pdone
        ST      r7, r6, CNT
        MOV16   r7, ZERO1
        JMP     shift
pdone:  LDI     r7, 2
        ST      r7, r6, STATE
text:   WAITB   INQ_NE, T                       ; TD has passed: a test, not a wait
        BT      idle
        .bounded "the WAITB INQ_NE, T just before completed by its condition, so INQ holds a word; only this thread pops INQ"
        POP     r7
        MOV     r3, r7
        SHRI    r3, 9                           ; C = bit 8: end of message
        BC      endw
        SHLI    r7, 9
        SHRI    r7, 9                           ; the character, 7 bits
        MOV16   r3, VTAB
        ADD     r7, r7, r3
        LD      r7, r7, 0                       ; code, 0, 0, stop 1
        JMP     shift
idle:   MOV16   r7, ZERO1                       ; nothing queued: idle
        JMP     shift
endw:   LDI     r7, 3
        ST      r7, r6, STATE
        LD      r7, r6, POST
        JMP     post
late:   CMPI    r7, 3
        BNZ     off                             ; 4: the ramp-down is over
        LD      r7, r6, CNT
post:   SUBI    r7, 1                           ; C = a symbol left
        BNC     down
        ST      r7, r6, CNT
        MOV16   r7, ONE1
shift:  SHLI    r7, 1                           ; C = the bit
        JMP     have
down:   LD      r7, r6, MODE                    ; postamble over: key down
        TEST    r7, r7
        BZ      off                             ; square: at once
        LDI     r7, 4                           ; shaped: th_m from rest to the
        ST      r7, r6, STATE                   ; envelope zero over N/2
        LD      r3, r6, RAMP0
        LD      r7, r6, KEYLEN
        JMP     shloop

; The varicode, one word a character 0..127: code, 0, 0, a stop 1, then
; zeros, left-aligned (tools.protomodels.psk31.left_aligned).
VTAB:
        .word   0xAAC8, 0xB6C8, 0xBB48, 0xDDC8, 0xBAC8, 0xD7C8, 0xBBC8, 0xBF48   ; 0
        .word   0xBFC8, 0xEF20, 0xE900, 0xDBC8, 0xB748, 0xF900, 0xDD48, 0xEAC8   ; 8
        .word   0xBDC8, 0xBD48, 0xEB48, 0xEBC8, 0xD6C8, 0xDAC8, 0xDB48, 0xD5C8   ; 16
        .word   0xDEC8, 0xDF48, 0xEDC8, 0xD548, 0xD748, 0xEEC8, 0xBEC8, 0xDFC8   ; 24
        .word   0x9000, 0xFF90, 0xAF90, 0xFA90, 0xED90, 0xB548, 0xAEC8, 0xBF90   ; 32
        .word   0xFB20, 0xF720, 0xB790, 0xEF90, 0xEA40, 0xD480, 0xAE40, 0xD790   ; 40
        .word   0xB720, 0xBD20, 0xED20, 0xFF20, 0xBB90, 0xAD90, 0xB590, 0xD690   ; 48
        .word   0xD590, 0xDB90, 0xF520, 0xDE90, 0xF690, 0xAA40, 0xEB90, 0xABC8   ; 56
        .word   0xAF48, 0xFA40, 0xEB20, 0xAD20, 0xB520, 0xEE40, 0xDB20, 0xFD20   ; 64
        .word   0xAA90, 0xFE40, 0xFE90, 0xBE90, 0xD720, 0xBB20, 0xDD20, 0xAB20   ; 72
        .word   0xD520, 0xEE90, 0xAF20, 0xDE40, 0xDA40, 0xAB90, 0xDA90, 0xAE90   ; 80
        .word   0xBA90, 0xBD90, 0xAB48, 0xFB90, 0xF790, 0xFD90, 0xAFC8, 0xB690   ; 88
        .word   0xB7C8, 0xB200, 0xBE40, 0xBC80, 0xB480, 0xC800, 0xF480, 0xB640   ; 96
        .word   0xAC80, 0xD200, 0xF590, 0xBF20, 0xD900, 0xEC80, 0xF200, 0xE400   ; 104
        .word   0xFC80, 0xDF90, 0xA900, 0xB900, 0xA400, 0xDC80, 0xF640, 0xD640   ; 112
        .word   0xDF20, 0xBA40, 0xEA90, 0xADC8, 0xDD90, 0xAD48, 0xB5C8, 0xED48   ; 120
